bedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7758, "total_tokens": 7758}}, "input": {"input": ["# SAP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technologies, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Operational Scope\n\nCloud Foundry is a key component of SAP's technology infrastructure, providing a platform for building, deploying, and managing applications. Its proactive approach to innovation and collaboration with other SAP departments helps safeguard SAP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective cloud management not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (330, 332, 333), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 04))]\n\n## Variant Configuration and Pricing\n\nVariant Configuration and Pricing is a critical component of SAP's technology infrastructure, enabling customers to configure and price their products according to their specific needs. Its focus on innovation and collaboration with other SAP departments helps maintain SAP's competitive edge and ensures compliance with regulatory standards. [Data: Sources (1602, 1603, 1604), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2025, 01, 22))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP's technology departments, established in 2025, ensures that technological innovations are compliant with regulatory standards and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (9, 332, 333), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 04))]", "# SAP Cloud Platform Update Overview as of August 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes within the SAP Cloud Platform as of August 2025. The information highlights the various components and their respective updates, focusing on the impact of these changes on the platform's functionality and user experience.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone has introduced several updates, including a change in the deployment timeline, starting from the 2507A release. The release to production will now take place on Tuesdays and Wednesdays every other week. Additionally, AI features such as text generation, summarization, and comment generation are now available in a preview environment. These features will be available until December 31, 2025, and will be offered as a promotional model. [Data: Sources (110, 330), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 23), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## Variant Configuration Updates\n\nVariant Configuration has introduced several updates, including the ability to set default values for characteristics, map new AVC authors, and persist user values involved in conflicts. These updates aim to improve the functionality and user experience of Variant Configuration. [Data: Sources (423, 312, 313, 314), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 23), (2025, 08, 13))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Update\n\nCloud Identity Services has migrated the data center in Saudi Arabia to the Google Cloud infrastructure. This update aims to improve the security and stability of Cloud Identity Services. [Data: Source (426), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 22), (2025, 07, 22))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Update\n\nContinuous Integration & Delivery has introduced an update that automatically selects the latest pipeline version when creating a new job. This update aims to simplify the job creation process. [Data: Source (315), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 12), (2025, 08, 12))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Update\n\nKyma Runtime has introduced an update that deprecates APIRule custom resource (CR) v1beta1 and schedules it for deletion. This update aims to improve the security and stability of Kyma Runtime. [Data: Source (316), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 12), (2025, 08, 12))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Related Services Overview as of July 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and related services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and related services as of July 2025.\n\n## SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nSAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime has been updated from version 49.4.0 to 50.1.0, enhancing its capabilities and performance. This update is part of SAP's ongoing efforts to improve its cloud-based offerings and ensure seamless integration with related services. Effective updates not only prevent technical issues but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 24), (2025, 07, 24))]\n\n## New Features in Application for Data Replication and Administration\n\nThe Application for Data Replication and Administration has introduced new features, including a new version indicator in the Getting Support screen and delta replication alerts for SAP CALM. These updates aim to improve user experience and ensure data integrity, underscoring the commitment to upholding high standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (3, 4), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 01, 22))]\n\n## Enhanced Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (5, 6), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 01, 22))]\n\n## Staged Deployment Strategy for Pricing Service\n\nThe Pricing Service has adopted a new staged deployment strategy, deploying new software releases to non-productive tenants first and then to productive tenants. This approach aims to minimize disruptions and ensure a smooth transition, underscoring the commitment to operational stability and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (7, 8), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 02, 05))]\n\n## Support for X.509 Certificates in Pricing Service\n\nThe Pricing Service now supports X.509 certificates, providing an additional security feature for customers. This update is part of SAP's ongoing efforts to enhance security and ensure the integrity of its cloud-based offerings. [Data: Sources (9, 10), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 01, 22))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Update Overview as of January 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and changes in SAP Cloud Services as of January 2025, focusing on the Pricing Service, Variant Configuration, Application for Data Replication and Administration, Cloud Integration for Data Services, Data Quality Services, and Kyma Runtime. The information highlights the importance of these updates in enhancing security, performance, and user experience.\n\n## Enhanced Security Measures\n\nSAP Cloud Services has introduced enhanced security measures, including the use of X.509 certificates for authentication, which is considered more secure than traditional client ID and client secret methods. This update is crucial for protecting sensitive data and ensuring the integrity of the system. [Data: Sources (1, 3), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 01, 22))]\n\n## Improved Performance and User Experience\n\nThe updates to the Pricing Service and Variant Configuration have improved performance and user experience. The new staged deployment strategy allows for more efficient testing and deployment of new releases, reducing downtime and improving overall system stability. [Data: Sources (2, 4), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 02, 05))]\n\n## Enhanced Collaboration and Integration\n\nThe updates to the Application for Data Replication and Administration, Cloud Integration for Data Services, and Data Quality Services have enhanced collaboration and integration capabilities. The new features and tools enable more efficient data replication, administration, and quality control, improving overall system performance and user experience. [Data: Sources (5, 6), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 01, 22))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Maintenance and Upgrade\n\nThe Kyma Runtime maintenance and upgrade will improve system stability and performance. The upgrade process will start in calendar week 04/2025 and will be completed in week 06/2025. The upgrade is a zero-downtime maintenance, and no actions are required from the user's side. [Data: Sources (7, 8), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 17), (2025, 01, 22))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and Data Services Overview as of January 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key components and services within SAP Cloud Foundry and Data Services, highlighting their relationships, operational scopes, and notable updates as of January 2025. The information is relevant to the company's technology and data management operations during this period.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Component Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has seen several updates and enhancements as of January 2025. These include the introduction of a new staged deployment strategy for the Variant Configuration service, starting with the 2502 release. This strategy involves deploying new software releases to non-productive tenants first, followed by productive tenants two weeks later. This approach aims to improve performance and reduce downtime. Additionally, the update mechanism for displaying errors relating to the SDI DP Agent has been corrected, and the alert for a too high number of deltas is now also sent to SAP Cloud Application Lifecycle Monitoring – Integration Monitoring. These updates demonstrate the company's commitment to improving the reliability and efficiency of its cloud-based services. [Data: Sources (1, 2, 3), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 02, 05))]\n\n## Data Replication and Administration Updates\n\nThe Application for Data Replication and Administration has also seen updates as of January 2025. These include the correction of the update mechanism for displaying errors relating to the SDI DP Agent and the enhancement of the delta replication alert for SAP CALM. These updates aim to improve the reliability and efficiency of data replication and administration processes. Additionally, the microservice now supports parsing point of reference data in Spanish South America countries, demonstrating the company's commitment to improving data quality and management. [Data: Sources (4, 5, 6), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 01, 22))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime has also seen updates as of January 2025. These include the upgrading of the Kyma runtime management in the Kyma Control Plane, which will involve temporarily duplicating ClusterRoleBindings of administrators. This upgrade is a zero-downtime maintenance and requires no actions from the user's side. Additionally, the telemetry module has been updated to version 1.31.0, demonstrating the company's commitment to improving the reliability and efficiency of its Kyma Runtime services. [Data: Sources (7, 8, 9), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 17), (2025, 01, 22))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes in SAP technology as of 2025, focusing on the components and services that have undergone significant improvements or new feature releases. The information is relevant to the company's operations and development efforts.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP has undergone several updates and improvements as of 2025, focusing on condition base calculations, validation fixes, and new features. These changes aim to enhance the service's accuracy, efficiency, and user experience. Effective pricing management is crucial for SAP's business operations and customer satisfaction. The updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to continuous improvement and innovation in its services. [Data: Sources (1487, 1488, 1489, 1490), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 17), (2025, 02, 05))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime at SAP has received several updates and improvements as of 2025, focusing on API Gateway, Telemetry, and LogPipeline resources. These changes aim to enhance the runtime's performance, security, and user experience. Effective runtime management is crucial for SAP's business operations and customer satisfaction. The updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to continuous improvement and innovation in its services. [Data: Sources (1484, 1485, 503), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 07, 09))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services at SAP have undergone several updates and improvements as of 2025, focusing on CAPTCHA protection, off-cycle upgrades, and new features. These changes aim to enhance the service's security, efficiency, and user experience. Effective identity management is crucial for SAP's business operations and customer satisfaction. The updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to continuous improvement and innovation in its services. [Data: Sources (501, 502), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 09), (2025, 07, 09))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and security. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP has undergone several updates to improve its functionality and security. The service usage used to be reported incorrectly if a PATCH request was sent via a POST request using the X-HTTP-Method-Override header. This issue has been corrected [Data: Sources (1486), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 31), (2025, 02, 05))]. Additionally, the condition base used not to be dynamically adjusted to account for the cumulative effect of prior conditions. Instead, all counters for the condition type used to use the original base amount. This issue has been corrected [Data: Sources (1487), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 17), (2025, 02, 05))].\n\n## Variant Configuration Updates\n\nThe Variant Configuration service at SAP has introduced several new features to enhance its functionality. A new endpoint called GET /api/v2/configurations/{configurationId}/items/{itemId}/characteristics is used to read the details of one or more characteristics of an item [Data: Sources (1481, 1581), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2025, 01, 22))]. Additionally, a new staged deployment strategy for the Variant Configuration service starting with the 2502 release has been implemented [Data: Sources (1582), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2025, 01, 22))].\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime component at SAP has undergone several updates to improve its functionality and security. The API Gateway module in version 2.10.3 includes the following changes: We’ve changed the hardcoded algorithm from RSA256 to RS256 [Data: Sources (1484), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 04), (2025, 02, 05))]. Additionally, the Telemetry module has been updated to version 1.32.0, bringing improvements such as a more sophisticated CRD defaulting mechanism [Data: Sources (1485), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 22), (2025, 02, 05))].", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's technology landscape, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations as of 2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP has undergone several updates, including the correction of service usage reporting issues and improvements to base calculations. These changes aim to enhance the service's accuracy and efficiency, supporting SAP's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1486, 1487), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 31), (2025, 02, 05))]\n\n## Variant Configuration Enhancements\n\nSAP's Variant Configuration has seen improvements, such as the correction of service usage reporting issues, the introduction of a new endpoint for reading characteristics, and the increase of variant table API limits. These updates aim to enhance the service's performance and user experience, supporting SAP's operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (1151, 1152, 1153), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 13), (2025, 03, 26))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nSAP's Cloud Identity Services have undergone several updates, including the addition of new features, such as bundle options documentation, central store logs display, and OAuth client authentication. These changes aim to enhance the service's functionality and user experience, supporting SAP's operational stability and innovation. [Data: Sources (1154, 1155, 1156, 1157, 1158, 1159), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 25), (2025, 03, 25))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance the company's operational efficiency and technological capabilities. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2025.\n\n## SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Updates\n\nThe SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing component has been updated to include a new type of price derivation rule, BenefitMultiplierPriceDerivationRule, as of Client API version 16.0. This update allows for the maintenance of a Loyalty Points Multiplier as a reward in the Maintain Promotions app. The update is effective as of 2025-01-22 and is part of the company's efforts to enhance its pricing capabilities. [Data: Sources (795), Date_Range ((2022, 01, 01), (2025, 01, 22))]\n\n## Variant Configuration Updates\n\nThe Variant Configuration component has undergone several updates, including the correction of issues related to the configuration service endpoint, AVC forwarding, and the inclusion of pre-defined characteristic values. These updates aim to improve the component's functionality and user experience. The updates are effective as of 2025-02-05 and are part of the company's efforts to enhance its configuration capabilities. [Data: Sources (1501, 1502, 1503, 1504, 1505), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 17), (2025, 02, 05))]\n\n## SAP Datasphere Updates\n\nSAP Datasphere has been updated to include new and changed features for administration and data modeling. The update is effective as of 2025-02-04 and is part of the company's efforts to enhance its data management capabilities. [Data: Source (1506), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 04), (2025, 02, 04))]\n\n## SAP AI Core Updates\n\nSAP AI Core has been updated to include new endpoints for the Pipeline API, allowing for the retrieval of information about documents within a pipeline, including processing status. The update is effective as of 2025-02-03 and is part of the company's efforts to enhance its artificial intelligence capabilities. [Data: Sources (1507, 1508), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 03), (2025, 02, 03))]\n\n## SAP AI Launchpad Updates\n\nSAP AI Launchpad has been updated to include an additional selected model from Aleph Alpha in orchestration. The update is effective as of 2025-02-03 and is part of the company's efforts to enhance its artificial intelligence capabilities. [Data: Source (1509), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 03), (2025, 02, 03))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded. The update is effective as of 2025-01-21 and is part of the company's efforts to enhance its identity management capabilities. [Data: Source (1608), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 21), (2025, 01, 21))]\n\n## Graph Updates\n\nThe Graph component has been updated to include improved visualization of actions and functions. The update is effective as of 2025-01-21 and is part of the company's efforts to enhance its data visualization capabilities. [Data: Source (1609), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 21), (2025, 01, 21))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has been updated to include best practices for capturing specific elements. The update is effective as of 2025-01-21 and is part of the company's efforts to enhance its process automation capabilities. [Data: Source (1607), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 21), (2025, 01, 21))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and development.\n\n## SAP AI Launchpad Updates\n\nSAP AI Launchpad has undergone several updates as of 2025, including the addition of new models from Aleph Alpha and enhancements to the grounding management app. These updates aim to improve the management of data pipelines and support the development of AI capabilities. [Data: Sources (1510, 1509, 1508), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 03), (2025, 02, 04))]\n\n## Variant Configuration Enhancements\n\nThe Variant Configuration component has received several enhancements as of 2025, including the ability to read variant table content and exclude globally assigned characteristics from configuration results. These updates aim to improve the efficiency and accuracy of variant configuration processes. [Data: Sources (1505, 1504, 1503, 1502, 1501), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 17), (2025, 02, 05))]\n\n## SAP Datasphere Updates\n\nSAP Datasphere has received several updates as of 2025, including new features for administration and data modeling. These updates aim to improve the management and analysis of data, supporting the development of AI capabilities. [Data: Source (1506), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 04), (2025, 02, 04))]", "# SAP Pricing Service Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP Pricing Service, highlighting its key features, updates, and improvements as of 2024. The report covers the Pricing Service's capabilities, including its support for various pricing scenarios, its integration with other SAP systems, and its ability to handle complex pricing calculations. The report also discusses the Pricing Service's updates and improvements, including its enhanced user interface, improved performance, and expanded functionality.\n\n## Pricing Service Capabilities\n\nThe SAP Pricing Service is a powerful tool that supports various pricing scenarios, including pricing for sales, purchasing, and other business processes. The service is designed to handle complex pricing calculations and provides real-time pricing information to support business decisions. The Pricing Service is also integrated with other SAP systems, such as SAP S/4HANA and SAP CPQ, to provide a seamless pricing experience. [Data: Sources (3001, 3004), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 25), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates and Improvements\n\nThe SAP Pricing Service has undergone several updates and improvements as of 2024, including an enhanced user interface, improved performance, and expanded functionality. The service now supports custom subtotal flags, data determination access type C, and KOMPAZAD, which are essential for businesses to manage complex pricing scenarios. The Pricing Service also provides real-time pricing information and supports various pricing scenarios, including pricing for sales, purchasing, and other business processes. [Data: Sources (3002, 3005), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 25), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## Integration with Other SAP Systems\n\nThe SAP Pricing Service is integrated with other SAP systems, such as SAP S/4HANA and SAP CPQ, to provide a seamless pricing experience. The service supports real-time pricing information and provides a single source of truth for pricing data, which is essential for businesses to make informed decisions and stay competitive in the market. [Data: Sources (3001, 3004), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 25), (2024, 05, 02))]", "# SAP Pricing Service and Governance Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP Pricing Service and Governance features, highlighting their key components, relationships, and notable updates. The information is relevant to SAP's technology and business operations as of 2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP has undergone significant updates, enhancing its functionality and user experience. Notable updates include the introduction of new endpoints, improved currency conversion, and enhanced determination of pricing attribute values. These changes aim to improve the accuracy and efficiency of pricing calculations, supporting SAP's business operations and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (596, 802, 803), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 16), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Governance Feature\n\nThe Governance feature in SAP Build helps establish rules for project creation and content transport, streamlining project management processes. This feature is beneficial for maintaining consistency and control over project workflows, supporting SAP's business operations and customer satisfaction. [Data: Source (805), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 21), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Substitution Management\n\nSubstitution management for SAP Build Process Automation tasks is supported in SAP Task Center, enabling users to create substitution rules for their tasks. This feature aims to improve the flexibility and efficiency of task management, supporting SAP's business operations and customer satisfaction. [Data: Source (808), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 21), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# Cloud Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key cloud services offered by SAP, including Mobile Services, Pricing Service, Cloud Identity Services, and Kyma Runtime. The report highlights the importance of these services in supporting the company's technology and innovation efforts.\n\n## Mobile Services Operational Scope\n\nMobile Services at SAP plays a pivotal role in providing a comprehensive platform for mobile app development, deployment, and management. The service offers a range of features, including offline support, push notifications, and security enhancements. The latest updates to Mobile Services, such as the introduction of new features and improvements to existing ones, demonstrate the company's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (591, 268), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 05, 01))]\n\n## Pricing Service Capabilities\n\nPricing Service at SAP is a critical component of the company's technology offerings, enabling customers to create and manage pricing rules, conditions, and scales. The service provides a range of features, including document pricing, return condition scales, and extension concepts. The latest updates to Pricing Service, such as the introduction of new features and improvements to existing ones, demonstrate the company's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (880, 591), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 25), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Importance\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP plays a critical role in providing a secure and scalable identity management solution for customers. The service offers a range of features, including groups, in-app help, and regular upgrades. The latest updates to Cloud Identity Services, such as the introduction of new features and improvements to existing ones, demonstrate the company's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (268, 509), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 11), (2024, 05, 02))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Capabilities\n\nKyma Runtime at SAP is a critical component of the company's technology offerings, enabling customers to build, deploy, and manage cloud-native applications. The service offers a range of features, including API gateway, application connector, and NATS module. The latest updates to Kyma Runtime, such as the introduction of new features and improvements to existing ones, demonstrate the company's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (268, 509), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 11), (2024, 05, 02))]", "# SAP Cloud Platform Technology Updates as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes in the SAP Cloud Platform Technology, focusing on the Pricing Service, Mobile Services, and other related components. The information is relevant to the company's operations and development around 2024.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP Cloud Platform has undergone several updates and changes, including the correction of issues such as missing exchange rates, proper displaying of exclusion indicators, and graduated interval scales factors. These updates aim to improve the service's accuracy and efficiency in pricing calculations. Effective pricing management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (94, 2066, 2067, 2068, 2069), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 24), (2024, 10, 23))]\n\n## Mobile Services Enhancements\n\nThe Mobile Services component has also seen significant updates, including the introduction of a Guided Tour for Mobile Network Trace, support for OData generated draft key values, and the ability to revoke user tokens for IAS. These enhancements aim to improve the service's usability and functionality, enabling customers to better manage their mobile applications and services. [Data: Sources (3571, 3572, 3573, 3574), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 17), (2024, 01, 31))]\n\n## Pricing Service New Features\n\nThe Pricing Service has introduced several new features, including the ability to return condition scales, distinct selects to database tables for local extensions, and the skip pricing extension implementations. These features aim to improve the service's flexibility and customization options, enabling customers to better manage their pricing strategies and configurations. [Data: Sources (3575, 3576, 3577), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 19), (2024, 01, 31))]", "# SAP Pricing Service Updates as of July 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes to the SAP Pricing Service as of July 2024. The report highlights the importance of these updates in enhancing the functionality and usability of the Pricing Service, particularly in terms of condition determination, pricing, and customization. The information is relevant to SAP users and administrators seeking to understand the latest developments in the Pricing Service.\n\n## Condition Exclusion and Determination Enhancements\n\nThe SAP Pricing Service has introduced enhancements to condition exclusion and determination, allowing for more accurate and efficient pricing calculations. The exclusion indicator (KONP-KZNEP) is now considered during condition determination, and standard requirement formulas have been updated to support this feature. This improvement is essential for ensuring accurate pricing and reducing errors in the Pricing Service. [Data: Sources (3, 4), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 28), (2024, 07, 24))]\n\n## Consideration of Cost Conditions as External Conditions\n\nThe Pricing Service now considers cost condition types as external conditions, where the condition rate must be passed by the caller to be considered. This change affects condition types with data sources other than Condition Technique and ensures that cost conditions are properly handled in pricing calculations. [Data: Sources (4, 5), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 28), (2024, 07, 24))]\n\n## Customizing API Enhancements\n\nThe Customizing API has been enhanced to return the scales order, allowing callers to determine whether scale rates must be passed in ascending or descending order. This improvement is crucial for developers and administrators seeking to customize the Pricing Service to meet their specific needs. [Data: Sources (5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 28), (2024, 07, 24))]\n\n## Document Pricing Enhancements\n\nThe Document Pricing feature has been enhanced to return the scales order, similar to the Customizing API. This change ensures that item conditions are properly handled in pricing calculations and provides developers with more flexibility in customizing the Pricing Service. [Data: Sources (6, 7), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 28), (2024, 07, 24))]\n\n## Extensions Concept and New APIs\n\nThe Pricing Service has introduced new APIs for testing local extensions, allowing developers to test and validate custom pricing routines directly. This feature is essential for ensuring the accuracy and reliability of custom pricing calculations and provides developers with more flexibility in customizing the Pricing Service. [Data: Sources (7, 8), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 28), (2024, 07, 24))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Updates Overview as of September 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and maintain regulatory standards. The information is relevant to the company's operations around September 2025.\n\n## SAP Task Center Updates\n\nThe SAP Task Center at SAP BTP has undergone significant updates, ensuring that service keys and service bindings follow the new pattern created after July 2022. This update is crucial for maintaining operational efficiency and regulatory compliance. The update also includes a deadline for recreating and updating service keys and service bindings by August 31, 2024. [Data: Sources (40), Date_Range ((2022, 07, 01), (2024, 08, 31))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP BTP has undergone several updates, including the consideration of cost conditions as external conditions, the return of scales order, and the extension of APIs to test local extensions. These updates are crucial for maintaining operational efficiency and regulatory compliance. [Data: Sources (43, 44, 45, 46, 47), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 28), (2024, 07, 24))]\n\n## SAPUI5 Updates\n\nSAPUI5 version 1.140 has been released for UI development and can now be consumed by SAP BTP services. This update is crucial for maintaining operational efficiency and regulatory compliance. [Data: Sources (63), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 03), (2025, 09, 04))]\n\n## Variant Configuration Updates\n\nThe Variant Configuration at SAP BTP has undergone several updates, including the return of all explanations for a conflict, the abort of explosion of incorrectly modeled BOMs, and the improved performance for possible values. These updates are crucial for maintaining operational efficiency and regulatory compliance. [Data: Sources (64, 65, 66), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 27), (2025, 09, 04))]\n\n## Content Agent Service Updates\n\nThe Content Agent Service at SAP BTP has undergone an update, including credential rotation. This update is crucial for maintaining operational efficiency and regulatory compliance. [Data: Sources (67), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 03), (2025, 09, 03))]\n\n## Cloud Integration Updates\n\nThe Cloud Integration at SAP BTP has undergone an update, including the IBM MQ adapter supporting a new version. This update is crucial for maintaining operational efficiency and regulatory compliance. [Data: Sources (68), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 03), (2025, 09, 03))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime at SAP BTP has undergone an update, including the telemetry module update to version 1.46.0. This update is crucial for maintaining operational efficiency and regulatory compliance. [Data: Sources (69), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 20), (2025, 09, 03))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_35d294c6d4331252ada1be2c8dd69f1ef5a629b95c1eeaf0934b023205b564db_v2"}